  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061z}{x+y}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061z}{x+y} & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061z & =c(x+y) \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(c(x+y))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of surfaces given by:\n\n$$\nz=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(c(x+y)),\\,c\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
